Actually it comes very close to making up for it.  I don't move
below Mines+Sokoban without 0 AC or better and I get that in the
mines.  A Wizard may need to purchase protection to acheive that,
but I test *all* armor at an altar for a b/u/c check until I have
at least 0 AC.  I try on *all* b/u armor to check for enchantment.
I do my best to identify all armor that might not be mundane.  In
particular I would want to check that padded glove for
power/dexterity/fumble.  Even +0 gloves of dexterity beat +0
leather gloves because of later potential.

> Maybe the reason I die so damn often is because I regularly wander around
> with around 4 AC after the mines?

Certainly.  May as well paint a target on your chest.

There is plenty of armor in the mines.  Check it all and exit the
mines with the best you found.  NOT with the first you found.
Consider several alternatives as well.  NetHack always offers
several right answers.  Speed boots vs jumping vs kicking.
Protection cloak vs MR.  You'll have at least one such choice by
the time you've checked every piece of armor you got in the mines.

Also at the altar once you're certain you are at max luck, it is
possible to wear every possible piece of cursed armor just before
praying and that way you can discover which possibly magical ones
are what.

